                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f15819cc-8f10-3141-a184-f68da7969aaa",
                        "entry_id": "5b99adbc-9897-3983-a6bf-7d8ee9f78e58",
                        "glosses": [
                            "внутренности убитого животного (желудок, кишки и т. п.); потроха"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "59578a80-33ba-4c93-a401-7ad21ed5a687",
                                "sense_id": "f15819cc-8f10-3141-a184-f68da7969aaa",
                                "text": "— Как же, хорошие, — сказал Никитин, — попадись ему только один на один, он тебе требуху выпустит."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d3f3f64-0ae0-464f-a4fb-2077adcb93b1",
                                "sense_id": "f15819cc-8f10-3141-a184-f68da7969aaa",
                                "text": "Длинные столы были завалены всякой требухой: бычьими печёнками, селезёнками и хвостами."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "96fe7f1d-774a-349b-acfe-823c435f590d",
                        "entry_id": "5b99adbc-9897-3983-a6bf-7d8ee9f78e58",
                        "glosses": [
                            "прост., перен., уничиж. нутро"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "88e799d6-c498-4d5e-96c8-2eaa7e26708f",
                                "sense_id": "96fe7f1d-774a-349b-acfe-823c435f590d",
                                "text": "Потому хоть ты и барин — да в кармане-то у тебя грош, а я, хоша и вторая гильдия, но могу тебя со всей твоей требухой купить."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4f20ba2-fd92-411d-a6d9-6d5fd232b466",
                                "sense_id": "96fe7f1d-774a-349b-acfe-823c435f590d",
                                "text": "Да я уверен, что за меня тогда, совсем с требухой, всего-то одну печёную луковицу дадут, да и то если с тобой в придачу!.."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "eb6698c6-04e8-4228-8788-ac4745b086e3",
                        "source_entry_id": "5b99adbc-9897-3983-a6bf-7d8ee9f78e58",
                        "target_lang_word": "chitterlings",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chitterlings",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c41c215-c23b-36e9-913d-db59894ae71f",
                                        "entry_id": "be367d64-7d34-322b-890a-9877019eea9f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Small intestine, cleaned and defatted, usually of a pig. Sometimes prepared with hog maws."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural",
                                            "plural-only"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01489be1-e0bd-4811-81da-2a7d6ed86730",
                                                "sense_id": "2c41c215-c23b-36e9-913d-db59894ae71f",
                                                "text": "How fare I? troth for ſixpence a meale, wench, as well as heart can wiſh, with Calves chaldrons and chitterlings […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "chitterlings",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a507b8c-5bb3-313e-9d1b-fb0bc6520b55",
                                        "entry_id": "e643c99f-c69f-3913-8733-816085fc3332",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "plural of chitterling"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bceb28cf-d5bc-4b2b-b481-b10e5559ed2e",
                        "source_entry_id": "5b99adbc-9897-3983-a6bf-7d8ee9f78e58",
                        "target_lang_word": "offal",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "offal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f3ac7cb3-be09-39fe-9bd6-9503b8592098",
                                        "entry_id": "a3c9ebdb-9cd2-3148-a1ab-b3a6d9e08044",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The internal organs of an animal (entrails or innards), used as food."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9f280de1-7697-38e4-8410-a7dc956a287a",
                                        "entry_id": "a3c9ebdb-9cd2-3148-a1ab-b3a6d9e08044",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A by-product of the grain milling process, which may include bran, husks, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a4271a0-2634-4a5e-ab86-f53616589e84",
                                                "sense_id": "9f280de1-7697-38e4-8410-a7dc956a287a",
                                                "text": "1817, John Taylor, Arator; Being a Series of Agricultural Essays Practical and Political in Sixty-One Numbers, Baltimore: John M. Carter, No. 32, Indian Corn, p. 96, https://books.google.ca/books?id=paMBAAAAYAAJ&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false\nThe whole of the corn offal is better food than wheat straw, but its blades and tops are so greatly superiour, that cattle prefer them to hay, and will fatten on them as well."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da8492a2-3e07-4a28-812e-88fdfe12af5b",
                                                "sense_id": "9f280de1-7697-38e4-8410-a7dc956a287a",
                                                "text": "Our standard wheat flour contains only the endosperm and represents practically a 75 per cent. extraction. The remaining 25 per cent. is known in the trade as grain offal or mill-feed, and is used largely as a concentrated food for live stock, being prized in the feeding of dairy cattle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "793a8eaa-7a48-49da-9fe2-9468e43d6f61",
                                                "sense_id": "9f280de1-7697-38e4-8410-a7dc956a287a",
                                                "text": "[…] the fragments are broken down and the finer particles are collected by sieving; finally, there is the bolting of the assembled fine fractions, with exclusion of the wheat offal which includes bran and a number of other commercial fractions like red dog and shorts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "98c9f9e7-ad1f-35e3-99da-9c1c76d5b577",
                                        "entry_id": "a3c9ebdb-9cd2-3148-a1ab-b3a6d9e08044",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dead body; carrion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d197cfed-e19f-39c6-be13-6cb780e979c7",
                                        "entry_id": "a3c9ebdb-9cd2-3148-a1ab-b3a6d9e08044",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That which is thrown away as worthless or unfit for use; refuse; rubbish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
